                    783.0,
                    858.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    858.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "When we read for pleasure, or when we're meant to follow the twists and turns of a writer's thinking or imagination, some uncertainty at the outset can be charming. For example, here are the first two stanzas of a poem by Emily Dickinson:",
